rash and/or personal injury.","remedy":"SET will notify owners, and dealers will inspect and tighten the affected bolts, free of charge. The recall began February 23, 2015. Owners may contact SET customer service at 1-866-405-4226. SET's number for this recall is SET-14B.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":3958,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=14V828000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":14,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"FJ CRUISER"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"LAND CRUISER"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"LAND CRUISER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2014","make":"SCION","model":"XB"},{"year":"2015","make":"SCION","model":"XB"},{"year":"2014","make":"SCION","model":"FR-S"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"FJ CRUISER"},{"year":"2015","make":"SCION","model":"FR-S"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"15V011000","received":"2015-01-16","manufacturer":"Southeast Toyota Distributors, LLC","component":"TRAILER HITCHES","summary":"Southeast Toyota Distributors, LLC (SET) is recalling certain model year 2013-2015 Toyota Rav4 vehicles manufactured June 1, 2013, to December 29, 2014, and equipped with an accessory trailer light module.  The software within the module may incorrectly detect an electrical short and preventively turn off the electrical current and the trailer lights.","consequence":"If the system incorrectly detects an electrical short and turns off the trailer lights while the trailer is being towed at night, there is an increased risk of a crash.","remedy":"SET will notify owners, and dealers will replace the trailer light module with a new unit with corrected software, free of charge.  The recall began on March 17, 2015.  Owners may contact SET customer service at 1-866-405-4226. SET's number for this recall is SET-15A.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1140,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=15V011000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":3,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"15V144000","received":"2015-03-13","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"STEERING:ELECTRIC POWER ASSIST SYSTEM","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain model year 2015 Camry, Camry Hybrid, Highlander, and Highlander Hybrid, and 2014-2015 Rav4 vehicles.  A component of the electric power steering (EPS) electronic control unit (ECU) may have been damaged during the manufacturing process.  Over time, this damage may result in failure of the electric power steering system.","consequence":"An unexpected loss of power steering increases the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the serial number of the EPS ECU or steering column assembly.   If the number is within the affected range, the EPS ECU will be replaced, free of charge.  The recall began on May 7, 2015.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-800-331-4331.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":110085,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=15V144000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V734000","received":"2023-11-01","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:12V/24V/48V BATTERY","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain 2013-2018 RAV4 vehicles.  Certain replacement 12-volt batteries may not fit properly in the battery tray, allowing the battery to move and contact the hold-down bracket, possibly causing a short circuit.","consequence":"A battery short circuit increases the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the battery clamp sub-assembly, battery tray, and positive terminal cover, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed December 27, 2024, to 2013-2014 RAV4 owners.  Additional owner notification letters will be mailed in phases, phase 2 will begin on May 14, 2025, and phase 3 in late July 2025.  Owners may contact Toyota's customer service at 1-800-331-4331.  Toyota's numbers for this recall are 23TB13 and 23TA13.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1853568,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V734000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
